Thus plan:

Step A: Create candidates.

Step B: Attach task profile to each candidate.

Step C: Confirm candidate preparedness for each.

Step D: Prepare origin and destination availability for leg assembly:
   - Assign operator to origin_availability_alpha (assign_operator_resource)
   - Activate origin node (activate_origin_node) (requires candidate_task_profile_linked)
   - Lock origin availability (lock_origin_availability)
   - Assign operator to destination_availability_alpha
   - Activate destination node
   - Lock destination availability

Step E: Assemble transport leg (assemble_transport_leg) using origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha (they are now locked and confirmed). This also requires transport_leg_available.

Step F: Authorize transport leg loading (authorize_transport_leg_loading) requires origin_availability_locked and candidate_task_profile_linked for origin_availability (we have). This will set loading authorized.

Step G: Now we can mark origin and destination availability dispatch ready:
   - mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready
   - mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready

Step H: Allocate vehicle units to origin and destination availability (if not already). We'll allocate vehicle_unit_beta to origin_availability_alpha, vehicle_unit_gamma to destination_availability_alpha.

Step I: Allocate dispatch slot to origin_availability_alpha (allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate) requires dispatch_ready ?candidate (we just made it), candidate_task_profile_linked, dispatch_slot_available, not dispatch_allocated.

Step J: Execute origin dispatch (execute_origin_dispatch) -> dispatched origin, vehicle available, slot available.

Step K: Allocate dispatch slot to destination_availability_alpha (now slot available again) and execute.

Step L: Allocate dispatch slot to shift_candidate_alpha (after we make it dispatch_ready via compliance path) and execute.

